Complete control flow

Think of the entire program like this:

                 main()
                   |
                   ↓
        Create Scanner object
                   |
                   ↓
              Read n = 5
                   |
                   ↓
           Create empty List
                   |
                   ↓
          Read 5 elements
                   |
                   ↓
       [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]
                   |
                   ↓
       simpleArraySum(ar)
                   |
                   ↓
             sum = 0
                   |
                   ↓
             for loop
                   |
        ┌──────────┼──────────┐
        ↓          ↓          ↓
      get(0)     get(1)     get(2) ...
       10          20          30
        ↓          ↓          ↓
      sum=10     sum=30     sum=60
        ↓
      get(3) = 40
        ↓
      sum=100
        ↓
      get(4) = 50
        ↓
      sum=150
        ↓
       return 150
        ↓
    back to main()
        ↓
   result = 150
        ↓
   print result
        ↓
       150
The most important thing to understand

There are two different loops doing two different jobs:

First loop:

for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    ar.add(sc.nextInt());
}

Its job is:

Take input and put the numbers into the List.

Second loop:

for (int i = 0; i < ar.size(); i++) {
    sum = sum + ar.get(i);
}

Its job is:

Go through the List and calculate the sum.

And the method call:

simpleArraySum(ar)

means:

"Take this List and send it to the simpleArraySum method."

Then:

return sum;

means:

"I finished calculating. Send the answer back to main()."
